Jokers.syn:
===[[Decks]]===
*{{d|Plasma}} benefits more from the large number of chips Blue Joker provides, which, when balanced, greatly boosts the score for the played hand.
*{{D|Green}} can encourage saving Hands or Discards, which can keep the Chips from Blue Joker higher during the round.
*{{D|Medusa}} and {{D|Monolith}} both work well with Blue Joker, as these decks both start with a {{J|Marble Joker}}, which means Blue Joker gains {{Chips|+2}} for free each blind.
*{{d|Five-Card Draw}}'s reduced hand size has slight synergy with Blue Joker since fewer cards are drawn to hand, meaning more cards remain in the deck, allowing Blue Joker to stay a bit stronger.

===[[Poker hands]]===
Hands that use fewer cards, are easier to draw, and have fewer base chips benefit more from Blue Joker:
* {{ph|High Card}}
* {{ph|Pair}}

===[[Jokers]]===
*Blue Joker naturally becomes more powerful as more cards are added to the deck and thus synergizes with Jokers such as:
** {{J|DNA}}
** {{J|Certificate}}
** {{J|Marble Joker}}
** {{J|Hologram}}

===[[Consumables]]===
*{{Spectral|Familiar}}, {{Spectral|Grim}}, and {{Spectral|Incantation}} add cards to the deck and thus increase the value from Blue Joker.

