In spite of its pitiful Mult bonus, Joker is a deceptively strong pickup in the early Antes due to its nature as an unconditional and extremely cheap score booster. It doubles the score of the most common 5-card hands at Level 1 ({{Ph|Straight}}, {{Ph|Flush}}, and {{Ph|Full House}}), making it so that every [[Blinds and Antes|Blind in Ante 1]] can be cleared with just one of these hands, provided the base Chips add up to 75 or more. Assuming the player spends {{Money|2}} in the first [[The Shop|Shop]] to buy Joker, buys/sells nothing else, and scores a sufficient 5-card hand (or {{Ph|Four of a Kind}}) in all three Blinds without using any more hands, they would enter Ante 2 with a minimum of:

* {{Money|19}} on {{D|Black}}
* {{Money|27}} on {{D|Blue}}
* {{Money|29}} on {{D|Green}}
* {{Money|40}} on {{D|Yellow}}
* {{Money|23}} on all other [[Decks]]

